  "question": {
    "text": "If \\(1, \\log _9\\left(3^{1-x}+2\\right), \\log _3\\left(4.3^{\\mathrm{x}}-1\\right)\\) are in A.P, then \\(x\\) equals",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jQU0s",
      "text": "\\(\\log _3 4\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e2BkP",
      "text": "\\(1-\\log _3 4\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ttx7C",
      "text": "\\(1-\\log _4 3\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hKFO9",
      "text": "\\(\\log _4 3\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text {Hint: } 2 \\log _9\\left(3^{1-x}+2\\right)=\\log _3\\left(4.3^x-1\\right)+1 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\log _3\\left(3^{1-x}+2\\right)=\\log _3 3\\left(4.3^x-1\\right) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 3^{1-x}+2=3\\left(4.3^x-1\\right) \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{3}{3^x}+2=4.3^{x+1}-3 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{3}{3^x}+2=12 \\cdot 3^x-3 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 12 \\cdot\\left(3^x\\right)^2-5\\left(3^x\\right)-3=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow\\left(4\\left(3^x\\right)-3\\right)\\left(3\\left(3^x\\right)+1\\right)=0 \\\\\n& \\because 3^x > 0 \\quad \\therefore 4\\left(3^x\\right)-3=0 \\\\\n& \\therefore 3\\left(3^x\\right)+1 \\neq 0 \\quad \\Rightarrow 3^x=\\frac{3}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\\)\n\\(\\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow x=\\log _3 \\frac{3}{4}=\\log _3 3-\\log _3 4 \\\\ & \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{x}=1-\\log _3 4\\end{aligned}\\)",
    "image": null
  },
